---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'August 13, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Search Stories Community Guidelines | findbyface"
  description="Rules for constructive, privacy-conscious Search Stories and replies on findbyface."
  canonical="https://findbyface.org/community-guidelines/"
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Community <span class="gradient-text">Guidelines</span></h1>
      <p>Help the next searcher without exposing or harming anyone.</p>
      <p class="page-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What Search Stories are for</h2>
      <p>
        Search Stories are first-hand experiences with the finders: whether a search helped, what
        kind of crop or image worked, what did not work, and what findbyface should improve.
        Constructive criticism is welcome. Helpful votes rate the usefulness of the advice, not the
        creator or performer.
      </p>

      <h2>What you may post</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your genuine experience using the finder.</li>
        <li>Practical advice about image clarity, cropping, lighting, angles, and screenshots.</li>
        <li>Respectful, specific product criticism and improvement suggestions.</li>
        <li>An established public performer stage name on the Pornstar Finder.</li>
        <li>A public creator username on the OnlyFans Finder, without connecting it to a hidden identity.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy and identity rules</h2>
      <p>
        Never post or infer a legal name, address, location, workplace, school, phone number, email,
        private social account, family relationship, or other identifying information. Never claim
        that a private person is an adult creator or connect an OnlyFans creator's public username
        with an offline identity they have not publicly established for that work.
      </p>

      <h2>Content we reject or remove</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Harassment, threats, stalking, hate, humiliation, sexual remarks directed at a person, or attempts to contact someone against their will.</li>
        <li>Anything involving or sexualizing a person under 18.</li>
        <li>Leaked, pirated, non-consensual, deepfake, or otherwise unlawful intimate material, including directions or links for finding it.</li>
        <li>Claims about private behavior, health, relationships, crimes, or off-platform sexual activity.</li>
        <li>Impersonation, spam, advertising, scams, payment or contact handles, repeated text, and irrelevant keyword lists.</li>
        <li>Links, images, embedded media, or code in Search Stories and replies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Moderation and reports</h2>
      <p>
        New stories and replies are reviewed before publication. We approve useful negative as well
        as positive experiences. We may reject or remove material that violates these rules, and we
        record moderation actions for consistency. Use Report on a published contribution for spam,
        personal information, a wrong or private identity, underage content, non-consensual content,
        threats, or harassment.
      </p>

      <h2>If a contribution is about you</h2>
      <p>
        Use Report for the fastest review, or send a correction or removal request through our
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Explain which contribution is involved and why it should
        be corrected or removed. Copyright complaints may also use our <a href="/dmca/">DMCA process</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
